{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01372",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.39,
      "end_seconds": 8.2,
      "duration_seconds": 6.81,
      "text": "Hello doctor, sorry, I took a wrong turn on the way here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 9.5,
      "end_seconds": 13.42,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "No problem at all, come in. What's troubling you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 15.19,
      "end_seconds": 20.54,
      "duration_seconds": 5.35,
      "text": "Okay, so doctor, I'm just here to help with the details."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 26.12,
      "end_seconds": 29.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "Please do. Extra information is always welcome."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 30.07,
      "end_seconds": 36.7,
      "duration_seconds": 6.63,
      "text": "I mean, he's been having sharp pain when I breathe in, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 37.52,
      "end_seconds": 41.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "When was the first time you noticed it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 43.07,
      "end_seconds": 46.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.65,
      "text": "I've had it for about two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 47.24,
      "end_seconds": 56.03,
      "duration_seconds": 8.79,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 56.99,
      "end_seconds": 63.44,
      "duration_seconds": 6.45,
      "text": "Deep breaths definitely sets it off. Honestly, a few times a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 64.38,
      "end_seconds": 67.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "Is there anything else with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 69.28,
      "end_seconds": 102.04,
      "duration_seconds": 32.76,
      "text": "It usually comes with a swollen painful calf. And sudden shortness of breath, too. The swollen painful calf? That's been for three days. As for swollen painful calf, I'd say mild. It happens once or twice a day. I've also been coughing up a little blood, since yesterday. About coughing up a little blood, I'd give it a five, out of ten. It happens all the time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 118.21,
      "end_seconds": 123.51,
      "duration_seconds": 5.3,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any chest tightness, wheeze or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 124.44,
      "end_seconds": 127.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "No, nothing to report there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 129.16,
      "end_seconds": 132.65,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "Any pins and needles or loss of strength anywhere?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 133.46,
      "end_seconds": 135.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "No weakness or anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.59,
      "end_seconds": 139.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "What about your medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 141.32,
      "end_seconds": 147.39,
      "duration_seconds": 6.07,
      "text": "Yes, high blood pressure. I've had heart disease for nearly five years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.09,
      "end_seconds": 150.55,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "Okay, go on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 155.21,
      "end_seconds": 157.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "Diabetes, for nearly five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 158.87,
      "end_seconds": 169.13,
      "duration_seconds": 10.26,
      "text": "Yes. Alright, heart disease, that matches what I have here. Has anything ever caused you a reaction? I mean any allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.35,
      "end_seconds": 172.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "Not to my knowledge, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 174.14,
      "end_seconds": 182.94,
      "duration_seconds": 8.8,
      "text": "Actually, I remember he had some kind of reaction to amoxicillin before. I couldn't swear to it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 184.41,
      "end_seconds": 187.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.67,
      "text": "Really? I don't think so."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 188.66,
      "end_seconds": 199.72,
      "duration_seconds": 11.06,
      "text": "Alright, so that's unclear. I'll record what each of you said. Alright, tell me about your routine, work, habits, that sort of thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 204.48,
      "end_seconds": 225.3,
      "duration_seconds": 20.82,
      "text": "I've never touched a cigarette. I used to drink heavily but I stopped four years ago. I grab fast food at lunch most days. I retired from the post office two years ago. Not much, I mostly stay in these days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.92,
      "end_seconds": 231.47,
      "duration_seconds": 4.55,
      "text": "Can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 232.81,
      "end_seconds": 253.27,
      "duration_seconds": 20.46,
      "text": "He is on hydrochlorothiazide, 12.5 milligrams, every morning for my pressure, I give it to him. He takes clopidogrel, 75 milligrams, once a day for the stent. He is on glibenclamide, 5 milligrams, before breakfast, I give it to him."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 255.19,
      "end_seconds": 259.54,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "I used to take ramipril, but I stopped it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.58,
      "end_seconds": 264.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "Okay, did you ever have any procedures done?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 265.47,
      "end_seconds": 271.48,
      "duration_seconds": 6.01,
      "text": "Just a mole taken off my arm, a few years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 286.7,
      "end_seconds": 289.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "Let me quickly check your readings."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 295.89,
      "end_seconds": 298.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "Sit still for a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 311.74,
      "end_seconds": 322.65,
      "duration_seconds": 10.91,
      "text": "Okay: respiratory rate 22, heart rate 102. And BP is 125 over 77, SpO2 94 percent on room air, temperature 37.5."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 324.41,
      "end_seconds": 328.69,
      "duration_seconds": 4.28,
      "text": "I'd like to check you over now, if that's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 329.23,
      "end_seconds": 330.79,
      "duration_seconds": 1.56,
      "text": "Yeah, no problem."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 332.76,
      "end_seconds": 334.57,
      "duration_seconds": 1.81,
      "text": "So, breathe out slowly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 352.26,
      "end_seconds": 358.95,
      "duration_seconds": 6.69,
      "text": "Your left calf is swollen and tender, and your oxygen is lower than I'd like."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 363.31,
      "end_seconds": 379.98,
      "duration_seconds": 16.67,
      "text": "You can relax now. Okay, so my impression is this: This looks most like a possible blood clot in the lung. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together. A chest infection is still possible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 387.58,
      "end_seconds": 411.58,
      "duration_seconds": 24.0,
      "text": "A CT scan of the chest is what I'd like next, for breathlessness. I want a D-dimer blood test done, that's for possible clot. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step. You need to go to hospital now for a scan. One warning sign to remember: you feel faint. In that case don't wait."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 413.14,
      "end_seconds": 416.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "Okay, I'll look out for that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 417.38,
      "end_seconds": 420.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "I'd like you back straight away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 420.98,
      "end_seconds": 423.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "Alright, I'll be back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 428.96,
      "end_seconds": 432.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 433.43,
      "end_seconds": 438.08,
      "duration_seconds": 4.65,
      "text": "Yeah, okay, that makes sense. Thanks for explaining."
    }
  ]
}